<title>USA: Barefoot up on ServiceMaster bid.</title>
<headline>Barefoot up on ServiceMaster bid.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Barefoot Inc rose 2-5/8 to 15-3/8 Thursday after ServiceMaster LP said it had agreed to acquire Barefoot for $16 a share.</p>
<p>&quot;It's an interesting fit, a good business fit,&quot; said an analyst who preferred not to be named. He said he could not comment on the offer price.</p>
<p>The two lawn care companies said the transaction was valued at about $230 million. They said Downers Grove, Ill.-based ServiceMaster's TruGreen-ChemLawn subsidiary is the largest U.S. lawn care company, and Columbus, Ohio-based Barefoot is the second largest.</p>
<p>Barefoot shareholders will receive the $16 a share in either cash or ServiceMaster shares. The deal is subject to regulatory approval.</p>
<p>ServiceMaster was down 1/8 at 24-1/2.</p>
<p>-- Susan Zimmerman, Cleveland Newsdesk 216-579-0077</p>
